version: 1.0.0
description: |
  Claude Code agent wrappers for the three Atelier content-generation
  personas (Quill, Lux, Iris). Each .claude/agents/<name>.md is a thin
  wrapper around the canonical persona definition under
  .paradigm/personas/<id>/. The agent files declare an MCP tool allowlist
  (real tool names from packages/mcp/src/tools/, plus the not-yet-built
  atelier_mind_map_query stub that ships in Phase 3 delegation B).
context:
  - 'Wrappers are inert markdown + YAML frontmatter only — no scripts (TD-229).'
  - 'Tool names use the Claude Code convention mcp__<server>__<tool>; the Atelier MCP server registers as "atelier" per packages/mcp/src/index.ts.'
  - 'The audio pipeline (trim, transcribe, captions) is NOT MCP — Iris shells out to the CLI verbs in packages/cli/src/commands/ via Bash and reads transcripts/*.json + cuts.json directly.'
components:
  claude-agents-bundle:
    description: The three Atelier content-generation persona wrappers (#quill-showrunner, #lux-cinematographer, #iris-composer) exposed as Claude Code invokable agents under .claude/agents/. Each wrapper references the canonical persona.yaml and system-prompt.md to prevent drift.
    file: .claude/agents/
  atelier-install-skill:
    description: Project-level skill (.claude/skills/atelier-install/SKILL.md) so Claude in a fresh clone of this repo knows how to install Atelier Design + Produce (pnpm install → pnpm build → atelier setup → atelier doctor) when the user-level atelier-design / atelier-produce skills aren't installed yet. Defers to atelier-design when that skill is available.
    file: .claude/skills/atelier-install/SKILL.md
aspects:
  agent-files-thin-wrappers:
    description: Every .claude/agents/<name>.md links back to its canonical .paradigm/personas/<id>/persona.yaml and system-prompt.md as the source of truth. The wrapper holds only the YAML frontmatter (tool allowlist, model preference, description) plus a body that mirrors the system prompt verbatim. Drift between the wrapper and the canonical definition is the antipattern this aspect guards against.
    tags:
      - convention
      - persona
      - source-of-truth
    anchors:
      - .claude/agents/atelier-quill.md
      - .claude/agents/atelier-lux.md
      - .claude/agents/atelier-iris.md
      - .paradigm/personas/quill/persona.yaml
      - .paradigm/personas/lux/persona.yaml
      - .paradigm/personas/iris/persona.yaml
    enforcement: wrapper references canonical persona; update both in the same delegation
    appliesTo: ["#claude-agents-bundle"]
  agent-tool-allowlist-matches-real-mcp:
    description: Every MCP tool listed in a .claude/agents/<name>.md frontmatter must resolve to an actual tool in packages/mcp/src/tools/ (verified by grep). The one intentional exception is atelier_mind_map_query, which is listed-but-not-yet-built — it ships in Phase 3 delegation B and Claude Code surfaces the missing tool gracefully until then. No persona may cite aspirational tool names.
    tags:
      - convention
      - integration
      - mcp
    anchors:
      - .claude/agents/atelier-quill.md
      - .claude/agents/atelier-lux.md
      - .claude/agents/atelier-iris.md
      - docs/keynote/paradigm/phase-3-reconciliation-notes.md
    enforcement: grep tool names against packages/mcp/src/tools/ before adding to frontmatter
    appliesTo: ["#claude-agents-bundle"]
